      "moduleId": "rn_6nfRDC4jtDHbdbqZ::L1",
      "stem": "Explain why a filtered solution rather than the whole crushed food is used for the tests.",
      "misconceptionClass": "filtration reason",
      "kind": "explain-why",
      "modelAnswer": "Reagents detect dissolved molecules, so the test must run on a true solution; filtering removes undissolved lumps that would cloud the tube, trap reagent and make the colour change impossible to read fairly.",
